// Every output of this function is drawn at its own bar, so the answer is 0.
//
// It takes the output's position among the outputs of [Core.CDLBREAKAWAY], from
// 0, and returns [BadParam] for an index that names no output.
func (c *Core) CDLBREAKAWAYDisplayShift(outputIdx int) (int, error) {
	if outputIdx < 0 || outputIdx >= 1 {
		return 0, BadParam
	}
	return 0, nil
}

// CDLBREAKAWAY recognizes the Breakaway pattern over bars startIdx through
// endIdx.
//
// A five-candle reversal pattern: a long first candle, a same-colored second
// candle that gaps away from it by its real body, two more candles extending
// the move, and an opposite-colored fifth candle that closes back inside the
// gap. Emits a bullish signal (bottom reversal) or bearish signal (top
// reversal).
//
// Formula and more info at https://ta-lib.org/functions/cdlbreakaway.
//
// Inputs, each at least endIdx+1 long:
//   - inOpen: Open price of each bar.
//   - inHigh: High price of each bar.
//   - inLow: Low price of each bar.
//   - inClose: Close price of each bar.
//
// Outputs, each at least as long as the values written (the input length always
// suffices):
//   - outInteger: +100 when the fifth candle is white (bullish breakaway), -100
//     when it is black (bearish breakaway), 0 otherwise.
//
// Element k of each output is the value at bar BegIdx+k of the returned
// [OutRange], and BegIdx is at least [Core.CDLBREAKAWAYLookback]: a range that
// ends before it returns NBElement 0.
//
// The error is [OutOfRangeStartIndex] or [OutOfRangeEndIndex] for a range
// outside 0 to [IndexMax] or ending before it starts, and [BadParam] for an
// input too short or an output empty or too short.
